course: dictionary
lesson: 6413
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one you need. «The perfume had a warm, musky smell.» Here musk means a strong, warm, animal-like smell, because the perfume is what has the smell.
explain: «The musk ox stood in a ring with its calves in the middle.» Musk is part of the animal's name here. The words ox and calves show you it is a real animal with a long, shaggy coat.
explain: Musk can also be a surname: «Musk is often in the news about rockets.» A capital letter and a person's name are the clues. Ask yourself: what does this word point to in the sentence? Then put your meaning back in and check it still makes sense.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Musk» can mean a strong, warm, animal-like smell.
fact: Musk was first taken from a gland of the male musk deer and used in perfumes; today most musk in perfume is man-made.
fact: Musk is used in the names of animals and plants with this smell, such as the musk ox, muskrat and musk rose.
fact: «Musk» is also a surname, the name of a person, so it has a capital letter.
exercise: «The perfume had a warm, musky smell.» What does musk mean here? | *A strong, warm, animal-like smell | A cold, sharp taste | A piece of old furniture | A loud noise from a big animal
exercise: «The musk ox stood in a ring with its calves in the middle.» In «musk ox», what is musk helping to name? | A month of the year | A town on the coast | A tool for garden work | *An animal
exercise: «Musk is often in the news about rockets.» What is Musk in this sentence? | A kind of plant | *A person's surname | A strong smell | An animal with a shaggy coat
test: «Musk oxen stand in a ring with their calves in the middle.» What do the musk oxen protect their calves from? | Frogs | Sheep | Perfume makers | *Wolves
test: Which of these is a plant name that uses musk? | Birch | Pine | Oak | *Musk rose
exam: Which phrase uses musk to mean a strong, animal-like smell? | *A musky perfume | Musk deer | Musk ox | Muskrat
